                <img src="/images/posts/postgres-skip-locked-vs-cas.png" referrerpolicy="no-referrer">
            </div><p>Eight workers poll the same <code>jobs</code> table. Each job must be processed by exactly one of them. Two PostgreSQL tools solve this, <code>FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED</code> and compare-and-swap (CAS), and on the same workload one claimed every job it tried for while the other lost most of its attempts.</p>]]></description></item></channel></rss>